<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ostrogoths</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ostrogoth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ostrogoths were the eastern branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a>, who lived north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and came under Hunnic rule in the late 4th century. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>' collapse they settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> as Roman federates, and in 488 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a> led them into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where they overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> and ruled from Ravenna. Their kingdom was destroyed by Justinian's armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War</a>, which ended in 554.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ostrogoths.jpg" alt="Ostrogoths" width="320" height="533" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: commons:Eulenjäger; derivative work by Newsleep · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomb_of_Theodoric_the_Great_Ravenna_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
